### DO-D8 handback: D9 restart inference
docs/delivery/handbacks/DG7/T-DG7-DO-D8-devops-engineer.md:15:| `deploy/scripts/transfer-drill.sh` | Sources the library. The EXIT trap stops both clusters with `td_stop_pg` and always ends with `true`. The source cluster at the D2/D3 boundary and the target cluster before the D9 restart are stopped with `td_stop_pg`; D9 fails if the target does not stop. The outer mode and the not-enough-disk BLOCKED path use `td_remove_work` instead of `rm -rf "$WORK"` | `c6cf2a1453f88cfbea1e875484944151788cd481e8478bf412c88e30b71f3d85` |
docs/delivery/handbacks/DG7/T-DG7-DO-D8-devops-engineer.md:27:- The same happened at the D2/D3 boundary for the source cluster, and in D9 before the restart. There, the old postmaster probably kept serving port 25433, so the new `pg_start` was most likely answered by the old server. I infer this from the mechanism; the pre-fix logs no longer exist to prove it. That is why I applied the fix to D9 as well and reran T-B11.
docs/delivery/handbacks/DG7/T-DG7-DO-D8-devops-engineer.md:79:- Step times in seconds: D0 193.968, D1 11.434, D2 1.899, D3 0.407, D4 6.963, D5 12.889, D6 3.246, D7 2.294, D8 33.808, D9 9.970 (the restart now preceded by a real fast shutdown), D10 0.863, D11 0.
docs/delivery/handbacks/DG7/T-DG7-DO-D8-devops-engineer.md:101:- Before this fix, the D9 "restart verified" claim in earlier runs (DO-D7, QA round 2 A18) probably did not restart PostgreSQL itself, because the old postmaster survived the SIGTERM sent to its subshell. Only the API and worker restarts were real. This is an inference from the measured mechanism; the old work trees and `pg.log` files are deleted. The T-B11 rerun here is the first one with a real PostgreSQL stop before the restart.
docs/delivery/handbacks/DG7/T-DG7-DO-D8-devops-engineer.md:105:1. For the orchestrator and qa-verifier: should the observation in the last bullet of §4 (earlier D9 restarts were probably API and worker only, not PostgreSQL) be recorded against A18/T-B11 evidence from earlier runs, and should QA's A18 rerun in round 3 cite this run's D9 instead?
docs/delivery/handbacks/DG7/T-DG7-DO-D8B-devops-engineer.md:42:| `deploy/scripts/transfer-drill.sh` | In the EXIT trap, after `td_stop_pg` for both pids, it runs `td_stop_pg_dir` for `$WORK/pgS/data` and `$WORK/pgT/data` (`\|\| true`; the trap still ends with `true`). At D2/D3 it adds `td_stop_pg_dir "$WORK/pgS/data" \|\| true`. In D9 the line is now `td_stop_pg "$PG_T_PID" && td_stop_pg_dir "$WORK/pgT/data" \|\| { echo "D9: the target PostgreSQL did not stop before its restart"; return 1; }`. | `8f651ba77266cfb4ee79b7eca36072fa29a82c93893b288a2e9735fb237b9e32` |
docs/delivery/handbacks/DG7/T-DG7-DO-D8B-devops-engineer.md:63:3. **D9 restarts the target PostgreSQL for real.** The new server starts only after the old postmaster, found by either route, has stopped. If it cannot be stopped, D9 FAILs with a named reason instead of connecting to the old server.
docs/delivery/handbacks/DG7/T-DG7-DO-D8B-devops-engineer.md:107:- **Drill result:** `transfer-drill: PASS in 272.677 s: 335 tables and 2 evidence files equal, origin http://127.0.0.1:25302, restart verified`. The D8 export package had 335 tables, 5006 rows and 2 attachments.
docs/delivery/handbacks/DG7/T-DG7-DO-D8B-devops-engineer.md:128:- DO-D8 inferred, and I agree, that D9 in drills before DO-D8 (DO-D7, QA round-2 A18) probably did not really restart PostgreSQL: the old postmaster survived the SIGTERM sent to its subshell. That cannot be proven now, because those work trees and `pg.log` files are gone. DO-D8's T-B11 and this one are runs with a real PostgreSQL stop before the restart.
